{#
  The insertion buttons for one automatic e-mail's declared variables
  (Core\Mail\Template\EmailTemplate, ARCHITECTURE.md §8.7bis).

  With `target` set, a click inserts `{{ '{{ nom }}' }}` at the cursor —
  in the subject field, and in the rich-text editor itself, which is a
  `contenteditable` rather than a text field: `public/assets/js/
  email-variables.js` handles both, because the caret is the caret.

  With `target` null, a click copies the placeholder to the clipboard
  instead — what the buttons on the page behind the editor do, for a text
  written somewhere else.

  Each button shows the French label; the placeholder itself and the
  example value are in the tooltip, so the row reads as prose rather than
  as a wall of braces.

  A required variable (EmailTemplateVariable::$required) carries
  « obligatoire » in the button itself, not only in the tooltip: the
  server refuses a text without it, and the only fair warning is one a
  touch screen shows too. The subject row passes `show_required: false`:
  the rule is about the body, and a badge there would say otherwise.

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/email_variable_buttons.html.twig' with {
      variables: template.variables,
      target: 'email-subject',   -- or 'richTextEditorContent', or null
      hint: 'Cliquez pour insérer…',
  } only %}
#}
{% set mark_required = show_required is not defined or show_required %}
{% if variables is not empty %}
    {% if hint is defined and hint %}
        <p class="form-label mb-2">{{ hint }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 email-variable-buttons"
         {% if target %}data-target="{{ target }}"{% endif %}>
        {% for variable in variables %}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
                    data-variable="{{ variable.name }}"
                    {% if mark_required and variable.required %}data-required{% endif %}
                    title="{{ '{{ ' ~ variable.name ~ ' }}' }} — exemple : {{ variable.example }}{% if mark_required and variable.required %} — obligatoire dans le texte{% endif %}">
                {{ variable.label }}
                {%- if mark_required and variable.required %} <span class="badge text-bg-warning ms-1">obligatoire</span>{% endif %}
            </button>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% else %}
    <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">Cet email ne prend aucune variable.</p>
{% endif %}
